@Scheduler_Api_HostAddress = https://localhost:7048

### Health check
GET {{Scheduler_Api_HostAddress}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

### Create an appointment — guest checkout, no login required (Name/Email/Phone identify
### the customer; a repeat Email+Phone is matched to the existing Customer record).
### Seeded Dealership id below is the one created by the InitialCreate migration.
###
### Correlation-id capture path: X-Correlation-Id is supplied below, so the middleware
### honors it verbatim — check the response headers, "X-Correlation-Id: local-dev-001"
### comes straight back. See architecture.md's Assessment Scope Notes for why this
### matters most in front of an API gateway/load balancer (none exists in this assessment).
POST {{Scheduler_Api_HostAddress}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: local-dev-001

{
  "customerName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "customerEmail": "juan@example.com",
  "customerPhone": "+639171234567",
  "vehicle": "Toyota - Vios - Vios G 2019",
  "serviceTypeCode": "OIL_CHANGE",
  "dealershipId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "technicianId": "33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333",
  "serviceBayId": "44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444",
  "startTime": "2026-09-07T10:00:00"
}

###

### Check availability for the slot just booked above — should report unavailable
GET {{Scheduler_Api_HostAddress}}/appointments/availability?dealershipId=11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111&technicianId=33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333&serviceBayId=44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444&serviceTypeCode=OIL_CHANGE&startTime=2026-09-07T10:00:00
Accept: application/json

###

### Check availability for a free slot (different technician/bay) — should be available
GET {{Scheduler_Api_HostAddress}}/appointments/availability?dealershipId=11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111&technicianId=55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555&serviceBayId=66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666666&serviceTypeCode=OIL_CHANGE&startTime=2026-09-08T10:00:00
Accept: application/json

###

### Same customer books again (different slot) — should reuse the Customer record from
### the first booking (same Email+Phone) rather than create a duplicate
###
### Correlation-id auto-generate path: no X-Correlation-Id header is sent, so the
### middleware mints one (Guid.NewGuid()) — check the response headers for a fresh
### "X-Correlation-Id" value that wasn't in the request.
POST {{Scheduler_Api_HostAddress}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "customerEmail": "juan@example.com",
  "customerPhone": "+639171234567",
  "vehicle": "Toyota - Vios - Vios G 2019",
  "serviceTypeCode": "TIRE_CHANGE",
  "dealershipId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "technicianId": "55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555",
  "serviceBayId": "66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666666",
  "startTime": "2026-09-08T10:00:00"
}

###

### Invalid: outside dealership operating hours (07:00, before 08:00 open) — expect 400
POST {{Scheduler_Api_HostAddress}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Test Customer",
  "customerEmail": "test@example.com",
  "customerPhone": "+639170000000",
  "vehicle": "Honda - Civic - Civic RS 2021",
  "serviceTypeCode": "OIL_CHANGE",
  "dealershipId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "technicianId": "77777777-7777-7777-7777-777777777777",
  "serviceBayId": "88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888",
  "startTime": "2026-09-07T07:00:00"
}

